 "description": "Start a NEW data question; preserve the user's wording, source, entity, period and requested deliverable. Use one call for multi-source supplier onboarding and due diligence, including ownership/controllers, filed accounts, VAT, directors/officers, screening, a combined PDF and a short summary. Never add latest, a year, freshness, a company number or a VAT number that was not requested or returned by a source. Returns one plan, total price ceiling or required clarification. No provider purchase. When approval_mode is chatbot, tell the person to approve in the card; do not ask for an extra yes/no answer or send them to an external link. Continue the SAME question through apiosk_execute with returned next_actions. Use English for Apiosk workflow messages, unless a translation is explicitly requested. Display Apiosk prices, charges and balances in the account display currency from context_view.money_display, using the converted prices supplied in the response. Raw proposal and billing amounts remain micro USD for authorization; never present those raw amounts as the preferred currency or override EUR with USD. Never change source document currencies. Output: this tool displays the complete result in an interactive card. After it, write only a brief confirmation (entity, source, period/date and optional unit caveat) and source citation. Do not add a second table, figures, costs, missing-data list or analysis unless the user explicitly requests those details. 'Show the result' or 'retrieve annual accounts' means display the card, not write a second report.",
